{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"xdrop","displayName":"Xdrop","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/xixu-me/skills/xdrop","publisherHandle":"xixu-me","publisherDisplayName":"Xi Xu","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/xixu-me","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1774563632963,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/xdrop/card?ownerHandle=xixu-me&version=1.0.0","sha256":"60faada372c6dc463d646f4abb17b34741751d90327476563e3ee432a7e50003","size":1679,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"5bcb9cca331509cad98dbcf2352f6268f34121d491f02c9eb55ee1a073767bf6","bundleFingerprints":["1e39dd1d2145017b5a1c287158d0be092a16770e1850408aae804880efb48664","f87ddf5832473076d57cd63f7404840e366cddb3d98924b176918bdd962830ed"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3107,"sha256":"f96fbb1d010b464442df22414661d785ba9fda89664d57b2fbbec83f8503e8dc","contentType":null},{"path":"scripts/download.mjs","size":10758,"sha256":"0cd22c54fff41b48094b34ea1aa8eb4fcc48415db8f50483579d6ad9fa654e8a","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/upload.mjs","size":20235,"sha256":"2900dccb6b69bf99f67cd62afc92ce9b1ac667cad9014b0af40ce3f62e37c5e4","contentType":"text/javascript"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"The skill is a coherent Xdrop file-transfer helper, but its downloader trusts server-controlled URLs and filesystem paths enough to create review-worthy network and overwrite risks.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789436749002,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Unrestricted Server-Controlled URL Fetching Enables SSRF"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/download.mjs"},"region":{"startLine":43,"endLine":51}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"91340db34ad1caaf"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/download.mjs:43-51`, `scripts/download.mjs:194-210`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Server-Side Request Forgery through unvalidated manifest and chunk URLs  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```js\nlogStatus(`Fetching transfer ${share.transferId}`)\nconst descriptor = await api.getPublicTransfer(share.transferId)\nif (descriptor.status !== 'ready' || !descriptor.manifestUrl || !descriptor.wrappedRootKey) {\n  throw new Error(getTransferStatusError(descriptor.status))\n}\n\nconst manifestResponse = await fetch(descriptor.manifestUrl)\nif (!manifestResponse.ok) {\n  throw new Error(`Couldn't load the encrypted manifest (${manifestResponse.status}).`)\n}\n```\n\nThe same trust issue affects server-provided chunk URLs:\n\n```js\nconst urls = await api.createDownloadUrls(transferId, chunks)\nconst urlMap = new Map(urls.map((item) => [item.chunkIndex, item.url]))\nconst noncePrefix = fromBase64Url(file.noncePrefix)\nconst fileHandle = await open(destination, 'w')\n\ntry {\n  for (let chunkIndex = 0; chunkIndex < file.totalChunks; chunkIndex += 1) {\n    const url = urlMap.get(chunkIndex)\n    if (!url) {\n      throw new Error(`Missing download URL for ${file.relativePath} chunk ${chunkIndex}.`)\n    }\n\n    const response = await fetch(url)\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe downloader obtains `manifestUrl` and individual chunk URLs from the selected Xdrop API server and passes them directly to `fetch`. It does not constrain the URL scheme, hostname, port, resolved IP address, or redirect destination.\n\nConsequently, a malicious or compromised Xdrop server can cause the process to issue HTTP requests to destinations other than the server the user selected. Potential targets include loopback services, private network hosts, link-local endpoints, and cloud instance metadata services.\n\nThe fetched content is subsequently treated as encrypted transfer data, and decryption should normally fail for unrelated responses. This limits direct disclosure through the Skill, but it does not prevent internal network probing or side effects caused merely by sending a request. Redirects may also move an initially acceptable request to a prohibited destination unless every redirect target is independently validated.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker operates or compromises an Xdrop-compatible API server.\n2. The attacker gives the user a share URL pointing to that server.\n3. The downloader requests the public transfer descriptor.\n4. The malicious API returns a `manifestUrl` or chunk URL targeting an internal resource, such as `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/...`, a private-network host, or a link-local metadata address.\n5. The downloader calls `fetch` on the attacker-selected URL from the Agent's network context.\n6. The attacker observes timing, status-dependent behavior, or application side effects to probe services that may not be reachable from the attacker's own system.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn attacker can induce unauthenticated GET requests from the privileges and network position of the process running the Skill. This may permit:\n\n- Probing loopback and private-network services.\n- Reaching link-local or cloud metadata endpoints.\n- Triggering state-changing endpoints that incorrectly accept GET requests.\n- Learning coarse service availability through errors, timing, or observable external behavior.\n\nThe code does not intentionally return fetched internal response data to the attacker, so the demonstrated scope is blind SSRF rather than unrestricted internal data exfiltration.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Permit only expected URL schemes, preferably `https:`.\n2. Restrict manifest and chunk URLs to an explicit allowlist of trusted storage origins.\n3. Resolve destination hostnames before each request and reject loopback, private, link-local, multicast, unspecified, and reserved IP ranges for both IPv4 and IPv6.\n4. Disable automatic redirects or validate the scheme, hostname, port, and resolved addresses of every redirect target.\n5. Where cross-origin object storage is required, have the trusted server advertise an administratively configured set of permitted storage origins rather than trusting arbitrary response URLs.\n6. Apply connection, response-size, and request timeouts to reduce network scanning and denial-of-service exposure.\n7. Consider routing downloads through the trusted Xdrop API instead of allowing the client to fetch arbitrary presigned URLs.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Symlink-Following Output Writes Can Escape the Destination Directory"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/download.mjs"},"region":{"startLine":56,"endLine":72}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"67b47d10d8c1878f"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `scripts/download.mjs:56-72`, `scripts/download.mjs:192-200`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Arbitrary file overwrite through symbolic-link traversal  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```js\nconst outputRoot = resolve(process.cwd(), options.output || `xdrop-${share.transferId}`)\nawait mkdir(outputRoot, { recursive: true })\n\nconst savedFiles = []\nfor (const [index, file] of manifest.files.entries()) {\n  const sanitizedPath = sanitizePath(file.relativePath || file.name)\n  if (!sanitizedPath) {\n    throw new Error(`Refusing to write an empty file path for ${file.fileId}.`)\n  }\n\n  const destination = resolve(outputRoot, ...sanitizedPath.split('/'))\n  await mkdir(dirname(destination), { recursive: true })\n  logStatus(`Downloading ${sanitizedPath} (${index + 1}/${manifest.files.length})`)\n  await downloadFile({\n    api,\n    transferId: share.transferId,\n    file,\n    rootKey,\n    destination,\n  })\n```\n\nThe destination is then opened in truncating write mode:\n\n```js\nconst urls = await api.createDownloadUrls(transferId, chunks)\nconst urlMap = new Map(urls.map((item) => [item.chunkIndex, item.url]))\nconst noncePrefix = fromBase64Url(file.noncePrefix)\nconst fileHandle = await open(destination, 'w')\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe downloader sanitizes lexical path components, removing `.` and `..`, but it does not verify the actual filesystem objects represented by those components. The calculated path can therefore remain lexically beneath `outputRoot` while resolving through an existing symbolic link to a location outside that directory.\n\nThe call to `open(destination, 'w')` follows a symbolic link at the final path and truncates its target. Intermediate directories can also be symbolic links because neither `mkdir` nor `open` establishes that every existing path component is a real directory beneath the intended output root.\n\nThis creates both a pre-positioned symlink attack and a time-of-check/time-of-use race if another local process can modify the output tree while the download is running.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker obtains the ability to create or replace entries under the selected output directory. This may occur through a shared directory, a previously created predictable `xdrop-<transferId>` directory, or another local process running concurrently.\n2. The attacker creates a symbolic link at the expected output filename, or creates an intermediate symbolic-link directory, pointing to a file outside `outputRoot`.\n3. A transfer manifest specifies a relative path that resolves to the symlinked entry after lexical sanitization.\n4. The downloader calculates a path that appears to be under `outputRoot`.\n5. `open(destination, 'w')` follows the symbolic link and truncates the external target.\n6. Decrypted attacker-controlled file content is written to the target using the permissions of the Agent process.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nA successful attacker can truncate or replace files writable by the operating-system account running the Skill. The scope is limited by that account's filesystem permissions, but may include:\n\n- User configuration and application data.\n- Shell or tool configuration files.\n- Project source files and build artifacts.\n- Other files accessible through writable shared directories.\n\nThis issue does not directly grant elevated operating-system privileges. Privilege escalation would require a separately exploitable privileged consumer of an overwritten file.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Create a new, non-predictable output directory with restrictive permissions and reject a pre-existing directory unless the user explicitly approves reuse.\n2. Inspect every existing path component with `lstat` and reject symbolic links or other unexpected object types.\n3. Open destination files with exclusive creation and no-follow semantics, such as `O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_NOFOLLOW | O_WRONLY`, where supported.\n4. Open and retain a trusted directory handle, then perform descriptor-relative operations so path components cannot be swapped between validation and use.\n5. Compare the canonical parent directory against the canonical output root immediately before writing, while recognizing that `realpath` checks alone do not eliminate races.\n6. Detect and reject duplicate destination paths after sanitization, including case-insensitive collisions on platforms with case-insensitive filesystems.\n7. Remove incomplete files after a download or authentication failure to avoid leaving truncated or partially written output.\n  ]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":50,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789436631.3580976,"endTime":1789436711.0154812}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"xdrop","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57d182qe5fv65enjqjdjkt1w18een3k-BbpeSI/clawscan-skillspector-3295868926/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-15T01:43:50.409193+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":43,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":80,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3107,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/download.mjs","type":"other","lines":389,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10758,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/upload.mjs","type":"other","lines":738,"executable":false,"size_bytes":20235,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-761cbfb5a63648b09b5c7fe58402a9ed","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":12,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/upload.mjs (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"- `scripts/upload.mjs` — Upload local files or directories to an Xdrop server and print the share link","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"371ffbca7cbecef75627141f57a62a9be5e59385cb04f3146fd3eb99bf4cd450","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":12,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-761cbfb5a63648b09b5c7fe58402a9ed","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":24,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/upload.mjs (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact loc